' How the picture on the right gets there.
'
' The one file here that draws with nothing but the jar: sequence diagrams are
' laid out by PlantUML itself, so this one comes back even on a machine with no
' Graphviz. The other three do not — which is half the reason for the image.

@startuml
title A diagram, drawn by something nobody installed

skinparam shadowing false

actor You
participant "Editor" as editor
participant "Preview" as preview
participant "container\n(or docker)" as runtime
participant "plantuml/plantuml" as image

You -> editor : type a line
editor -> preview : the text changed

note right of preview
  Debounced. Drawing means starting a JVM,
  and a diagram per keystroke would mean
  a JVM per keystroke.
end note

preview -> runtime : run --rm -i plantuml/plantuml:1.2026.6 -pipe -tpng
activate runtime
runtime -> image : start
activate image

preview -> image : @startuml … @enduml, on stdin
image --> preview : PNG, on stdout
deactivate image
runtime --> preview : exit 0
deactivate runtime

preview -> You : the drawing

note over preview, image
  Nothing is mounted. The container never sees the
  project — only the text of this one file — and
  nothing is written beside the source either.

  UTF-8 both ways, so „Größe" arrives as „Größe".
end note

@enduml
